NEARS-1089 task_bug: signal-collision — traces export failure is silently swallowed
Root cause: Admin/app/Observability/OtelDiagnosticLogger.php:96
  $dedupeKey = $level . "|" . $message . "|" . ($errorType ?? "");   <-- signal NOT in key

LIVE EVIDENCE A — 117 requests driven against a REFUSED collector (130s):
  export-failure lines emitted : 117
  distinct signals in them     : 117x "signal":"metrics"   (0x traces)
  but condition-D listener proves BOTH signals are real: 19x /v1/traces + 19x /v1/metrics
  => ~234 fault events occurred, 117 were logged, 117 traces drops were never reported.

LIVE EVIDENCE B — minimal repro, 2 distinct-signal faults in ONE process:
  $l->log("error","Export failure",[exception=>$e, source=>"...Otlp\MetricExporter"]);
  $l->log("error","Export failure",[exception=>$e, source=>"...SpanProcessor\BatchSpanProcessor"]);
  emitted lines: 1   ->   "signal":"metrics","suppressed_since_last":0
  expected     : 2   ->   one metrics line AND one traces line

Impact: during a collector outage the log always names signal=metrics; the dropped TRACES
batch (the primary signal for this app: OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp) is collapsed into the
metrics line and its count is discarded at request end. An operator reading laravel.log
would conclude only metrics exports are failing. AC4's four required fields are all present,
so AC4 passes literally, but the 'signal' field is unreliable.
Fix: include the signal (or $context['source']) in the dedupe key.
